# Byte-compiled output. Python writes these beside every module, so without
# Editor, tooling and patch leftovers.
# MEMORY_GLOBS in jarvis_os/selfupdate.py, so this is defence in depth.
# Offline model caches: multi-GB and re-downloadable, never committed.
# Persistent memory and audit ledger, never committed. Also excluded by
# Runtime logs and one-off test artefacts.
# Scratch directories.
# Secrets and local-only config.
# Volatile runtime state.
# machine-local agent/tooling config, not part of the shipped kernel
# selftest.py output. It snapshots the whole worktree on every run, so without
# them each run drops compiled artefacts into git history.
# these the snapshot would sweep its own output back into the commit.
*$py.class
*.bak
*.key
*.orig
*.py[cod]
*.rej
*.tmp
*~
.scratch/
__pycache__/
config.json
data/**/*.log
data/.selftest_baseline.json
data/.selftest_scratch/
data/actions.jsonl
data/audit.db*
data/audit_ledger.jsonl
data/control.token
data/heartbeat.json
data/jarvis_daemon.log
data/langcache/
data/lessons.jsonl
data/memory.db
data/memory.db-*
data/models/
data/selftest_run*.err
data/selftest_run*.log
data/smoke.txt
data/vectors.json
data/vectors.json.tmp
opencode.json
scratch/
temp/
tmp/
